Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:00:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] Bluetooth: hci_qca: allow the SLIMbus HFP offload on
 WCN6750 too

The Nothing Phone (1) carries SCO over SLIMbus to the DSP like surya's WCN3990 (the stock firmware
routes Bluetooth calls through SLIMBUS_7). Let the hfp_offload parameter enable it there as well; it
stays off by default.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
index ce4e3c38c..bdfa298cc 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -2630,7 +2630,8 @@ static int qca_serdev_probe(struct serdev_device *serdev)
 			hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_LE_STATES);
 
 		if ((data->capabilities & QCA_CAP_HFP_HW_OFFLOAD) ||
-		    (hfp_offload && data->soc_type == QCA_WCN3990))
+		    (hfp_offload && (data->soc_type == QCA_WCN3990 ||
+				     data->soc_type == QCA_WCN6750)))
 			qcadev->support_hfp_hw_offload = true;
 	}
 
